      "time": "4:05 - 5:10",
      "duration_seconds": 65,
      "narrative": "Let me go back and show you the fine-tuned model. This is the model right here that we fine-tuned. You can see that as we monitor it, it got progressively better until I did an eval. And remember, this is the one we did with the agent optimizer. Did we do just as good with the actual fine-tuned model? Let's take a look. We surely did. In fact, let me go back to my GitHub copilot because I actually told it to compare them side by side. Notice that it actually did 81.7% with the 5.5 and the optimized agent. It did 82.5% with the same optimized assets and the new tiny model, but the cost comparison is where it really comes through. Take a look at this. We can get an estimated almost 70% savings with this brand new model. And again, I don't know. I did this all agentically myself, well, with the agent. So there you go. I showed you how to actually tune your agent to be better first on accuracy with a big model, and then we swapped out that model and still maintain the accuracy with fine-tuning.",
